{
  "case_id": "2021-20-979",
  "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Patel",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Patel argued before an Immigration Judge that he had mistakenly checked the \u201cciti- zen\u201d box on the state application and thus lacked the subjective intent necessary to violate the federal statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Patel",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Patel petitioned the Eleventh Circuit for review, where a panel of that court held that it lacked jurisdiction to consider his claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government argues that it refers exclusively to a decision requiring the use of discretion, which the factual fndings in this case are not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0000-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a dissenting opinion, in which Breyer, Sotomayor, and Kagan, JJ., joined, post, p. 347."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Immigration Judge",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0000-0008",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judge accordingly denied Patel's application for adjustment of status and ordered that he and his wife be removed from the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government argues that, at least when used outside the context of a fnal judgment of a court, \u201cjudgment\u201d does not refer to just any decision. According to the Government, \u00a7 1252(a)(2)(B)(i)'s use of \u201cjudgment\u201d refers exclusively to a decision that requires the use of discretion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Patel",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Patel agrees with the Government that \u201cjudgment\u201d implies an exercise of discretion, but unlike the Government, he would not sift through eligibility determinations to classify them as discretionary or nondiscretionary. Instead, Patel reads the phrase \u201cregarding the granting of relief\u201d to focus the jurisdictional bar narrowly on a single discretionary judgment: the immigration judge's decision whether to grant relief to an applicant eligible to receive it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0001-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\u00a7 1252(a)(2)(B)(i) does not stop at just the grant or denial of relief; it extends to any judgment \u201cregarding\u201d that ultimate decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0001-0004",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Federal courts lack jurisdiction to review facts found as part of discretionary-relief proceedings under \u00a7 1255 and the other provisions enumerated in \u00a7 1252(a)(2)(B)(i). We therefore affrm the judgment of the Court of Appeals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0002-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is a bold claim promising dire consequences for countless lawful immigrants. And it is such an unlikely assertion of raw administrative power that not even the agency that allegedly erred, nor any other arm of the Executive Branch, endorses it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court-appointed amicus",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It depends on a Court-appointed amicus who offers arguments for the government that even the government refuses to advance on its own behalf."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-979",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "995bbf062026d06e4def821c25269e4d66e69f9be268b00d9c3a68b285067c8d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-995bbf062026-0003-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "decisions invested to the Attorney General's discretion, not antecedent statutory eligibility determinations."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
